      "extract": "A partition $\\lambda$ of $n$ is a non-increasing sequence $\\lambda= (\\lambda_1, \\lambda_2, \\ldots, \\lambda_\\ell)$ of positive integers that add up to $n$. We refer to the integers $\\lambda_i$ as the parts of $\\lambda$. As usual, we denote by $p(n)$ the number of partitions of $n$. Since the empty partition $\\emptyset$ is the only partition of $0$, we have $p(0)=1$. For a thorough introduction to the theory of",
