      "extract": "[]{#distinct-reg label=\"distinct-reg\"} Proving identities (6.8), (6.9), (6.11), and (6.14) in [@M1] combinatorially is still an open problem. The difficulty consists in finding a combinatorial proof of the Weierstrass addition formula [@KMR Identity (8.1)] used in [@KMR] to prove these identities. In this section, we use the Weierstrass addition formula to prove Theorem [\\[d5\\]](#d5){reference-type=\"ref\"",
